 <h2 id="check">Check your understanding</h2>
 <details><summary>The ship reports a 2,000 ft ceiling and 5 miles. Which case, and how will you recover?</summary><p>Case II: a controlled descent through the cloud to the break, then the normal visual pattern.</p></details>
 <details><summary>Why is the carrier pattern flown parallel to the ship's heading when the landing area is angled?</summary><p>The pattern is set from the BRC; the angled deck's centerline, the final bearing, is about 10° off it, and you line up on it as you roll into the groove.</p></details>
 <details><summary>Your hook catches a wire. When do you reduce power?</summary><p>Only when the jet has stopped and the yellow shirt signals power back. You go to full power on touchdown in case of a bolter.</p></details>
 <details><summary>The ball is 20 ft high at a mile, then 20 ft high just short of the ramp. Why does the second look so much worse?</summary><p>The lens's light is a wedge: 20 ft at a mile is a small angle, but the same 20 ft near the ramp is several times the angle and can put the ball off the top of the lens.</p></details>
 <details><summary>What do the cut and waveoff lights mean when they flash alternately?</summary><p>Bingo: go to your divert field.</p></details>
 <details><summary>A helicopter on final loses sight of the LSE. What now?</summary><p>Wave off, call “waving off” parallel to the BRC and re-enter the pattern.</p></details>
 <details><summary>Which LSE signals must a helicopter pilot obey?</summary><p>Wave-off and hold. The others are advisory.</p></details>
 <details><summary>Under FM 1-564, an Army pilot last made four single-spot landings 120 days ago. Current?</summary><p>No, but within 180 days: a refresher with a current DLQ pilot, 4 field deck landings and then 6 shipboard landings within ten days.</p></details>
 <details><summary>Why does an AV-8B make a short takeoff instead of a vertical one when it carries a full load?</summary><p>It can only lift off vertically below its maximum weight. A short takeoff adds wing lift to jet lift and lets it carry much more fuel and weapons.</p></details>

